From f14509b223979c323669e50bb71584740dec0a2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:46:32 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 095/128] render: a keyframe timeline follows its parent's
 (options.parent)

WE's binding parser reads an animation's `options.parent.key` (GH 0x1401d1740, B2's G01 row); the
editor writes it on the property whose timeline follows a sibling's, with `options.children`
listing them back on the parent. 5 library scenes use it: 1864677589's origins follow their
angles, 3163060610's scripted Radius timeline (startpaused, played by its script) drives Size and
opacity, which ran on their own clocks at load instead of waiting for it.

The parser now records each animation with the JSON object holding it (an object, an effect
pass's constantshadervalues) and its key; once the scene is parsed, a child is linked to the
parentless sibling its parent.key names. A child's time is the parent's (seconds, held at its own
length), advanced after the parents each frame. Inferred: the shared clock (the runtime's use of
the link wasn't read).

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md "Leftovers result" (B2's shared parent/children timelines)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
